About StarRez

StarRez is the global leader in student housing software, providing innovative solutions for on and off-campus housing management, resident wellness and experience, and revenue generation. Trusted by 1,400+ clients across 25+ countries, StarRez supports more than 4 million beds annually with its user-friendly, all-in-one platform, delivering seamless experiences for students and administrators. With offices in the United States, Australia, the UK, and India, StarRez blends the robust capabilities of a global organization with the personalized care and service of a trusted partner.

The Role   &nbsp;

As an UI/UX Designer, you’ll &nbsp;own the design of complex, data ‑ rich experiences that support decision ‑ making for administrators and improve clarity and usability across our platform. &nbsp;

You’ll &nbsp;work as a senior individual contributor within a cross ‑ functional product team :&nbsp; Design, Product, Engineering, bringing deep UI/UX&nbsp; expertise &nbsp;to your product area. While Product Management owns roadmap direction and prioritisation, you will play a critical role in informing decisions through research, design exploration, and user ‑ centred evidence, translating complexity into intuitive, accessible solutions. &nbsp;

This role sits within a newly established team focused on analytics, dashboards, and reporting, where&nbsp; you’ll &nbsp;elevate usability, interaction design, and data visualisation quality across&nbsp; StarRez &nbsp;products. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

What You Will Own &nbsp;

• Lead complex design initiatives from discovery through delivery, translating multi ‑ role, data ‑ heavy workflows into intuitive, scalable, and accessible experiences. &nbsp;

• Conduct and contribute to continuous discovery activities, including customer interviews, usability testing, and concept validation, surfacing insights that inform product decisions and reduce delivery risk. &nbsp;

• Partner with Product to support clear problem framing, hypotheses, and measures of success, using research, experimentation, and customer feedback to&nbsp;validate&nbsp;design decisions and iterate solutions. &nbsp;

• Work iteratively, shipping improvements in stages and refining designs based on real ‑ world usage, feedback, and&nbsp;observed&nbsp;outcomes. &nbsp;

• Elevate data visualisation quality across dashboards and reporting experiences, ensuring information is clear, meaningful, and usable for diverse audiences. &nbsp;

• Strengthen the broader product experience by contributing to our design system and embedding accessibility best practices (WCAG 2.2 AA) in collaboration with Engineering. &nbsp;

• Support stakeholder alignment through clear communication of UX decisions, improving usability and consistency through hands ‑ on critique, shared UI/UX patterns, and informal mentorship. &nbsp;

• Actively&nbsp;leverage&nbsp;AI ‑ powered tools and workflows within the design practice to accelerate exploration, iteration, and problem ‑ solving.  &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Required Qualifications &nbsp;

• 5+ years of experience designing complex SaaS or B2B digital products. &nbsp;

• Strong experience designing&nbsp;data ‑ rich&nbsp;interfaces, including dashboards, reporting tools, or complex operational systems.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience contributing to measurable product or business impact through improved usability, efficiency, or user satisfaction. &nbsp;

• Strong systems thinking and experience working across interconnected workflows or multi-role platforms. &nbsp;

• Proficiency&nbsp;in interaction design, information architecture, and high-fidelity execution. &nbsp;

• Experience leading discovery efforts and synthesizing insights into actionable product decisions. &nbsp;

• Strong communication&nbsp;skills and the ability to articulate design rationale clearly to cross-functional stakeholders. &nbsp;

• Experience partnering closely with Engineering to ensure high-quality implementation. &nbsp;

